# V1 Server Actions & Authentication

Follow these patterns for Server Actions and authentication used in the V1 codebase.

## 🔐 **Safe Action Pattern**

All Server Actions use [next-safe-action](https://next-safe-action.dev) for validation. Reference: [apps/app/src/actions/safe-action.ts](mdc:apps/app/src/actions/safe-action.ts)

```typescript
import { z } from "zod";
import { authActionClient } from "../safe-action";

// 1. Define schema
const updatePostSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  title: z.string().min(1),
  content: z.string(),
});

// 2. Create action with metadata
export const updatePostAction = authActionClient
  .schema(updatePostSchema)
  .metadata({
    name: "update-post",
    track: {
      event: "Post Updated",
      channel: "dashboard",
    },
  })
  .action(async ({ parsedInput, ctx }) => {
    const { id, title, content } = parsedInput;
    const { user, supabase } = ctx;

    // Early validation
    if (!user) {
      throw new Error("Unauthorized");
    }

    // Database operation
    const { data, error } = await supabase
      .from("posts")
      .update({ title, content })
      .eq("id", id)
      .eq("user_id", user.id)
      .select()
      .single();

    if (error) {
      throw new Error("Failed to update post");
    }

    return { post: data };
  });
```

## 🏗️ **Action Clients**

Use the appropriate client based on authentication needs:

- **`actionClient`** - Basic actions without auth
- **`authActionClient`** - Authenticated actions with:
  - Rate limiting via `@v1/kv/ratelimit`
  - User context from Supabase auth
  - Analytics tracking via `@v1/analytics`
  - Sentry error monitoring

## 📁 **File Organization**

Store actions in [apps/app/src/actions](mdc:apps/app/src/actions):

```
actions/
├── safe-action.ts          # Action clients setup
├── post/
│   ├── schema.ts          # Zod schemas
│   └── update-action.ts   # Action implementation
└── user/
    ├── schema.ts
    └── profile-action.ts
```

## 🔍 **Error Handling**

```typescript
// Model expected errors as return values
export const createPostAction = authActionClient
  .schema(createPostSchema)
  .action(async ({ parsedInput, ctx }) => {
    try {
      // Action logic
      return { success: true, post: data };
    } catch (error) {
      // Log error but don't expose details
      logger.error("Create post failed", error);
      return { success: false, error: "Failed to create post" };
    }
  });
```

## 🚀 **Usage in Components**

```typescript
"use client";
import { useAction } from "next-safe-action/hooks";
import { updatePostAction } from "@/actions/post/update-action";

export function PostForm() {
  const { execute, result, isExecuting } = useAction(updatePostAction);

  const handleSubmit = async (formData: FormData) => {
    execute({
      id: formData.get("id") as string,
      title: formData.get("title") as string,
      content: formData.get("content") as string,
    });
  };

  return (
    <form action={handleSubmit}>
      {/* Form fields */}
      <button disabled={isExecuting}>
        {isExecuting ? "Saving..." : "Save"}
      </button>
    </form>
  );
 }
 ```
